# REST-client smoke tests against `wrangler dev` (http://localhost:8787).
# Fill in @adminSecret and run top to bottom.
@base = http://localhost:8787
@adminSecret = changeme

### Health
GET {{base}}/v1/health

### Mint an account
POST {{base}}/v1/admin/users
X-Admin-Secret: {{adminSecret}}
content-type: application/json

{"email":"me@example.com","password":"test1234","label":"Me"}

### Login  → copy .token into @token below
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/login
content-type: application/json

{"email":"me@example.com","password":"test1234","device":"macbook","platform":"macos"}

@token = PASTE_TOKEN

### Push two ops + pull
POST {{base}}/v1/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{"cursor":0,"epoch":0,"ops":[
  {"ns":"prog","k":"movie:dune","v":{"p":300000,"d":9000000,"w":0},"deleted":false,"updated_at":1755600000000},
  {"ns":"fav","k":"movie:dune","v":{"at":1755600000000},"deleted":false,"updated_at":1755600000000}
]}

### Retry the same push — results ok:true, but cursor must NOT advance
POST {{base}}/v1/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{"cursor":2,"epoch":0,"ops":[
  {"ns":"prog","k":"movie:dune","v":{"p":300000,"d":9000000,"w":0},"deleted":false,"updated_at":1755600000000}
]}

### Stale write — expect ok:false with current doc inlined
POST {{base}}/v1/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{"cursor":2,"epoch":0,"ops":[
  {"ns":"prog","k":"movie:dune","v":{"p":1,"d":9000000,"w":0},"deleted":false,"updated_at":1000000000000}
]}

### TV pairing: start (unauthed), approve (authed), poll
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/pair/start
content-type: application/json

{"device":"Fire TV","platform":"tv"}

### Devices
GET {{base}}/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Catalog home (needs TMDB_KEY secret in dev: wrangler dev --var TMDB_KEY:...)
GET {{base}}/v1/catalog/home
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
